            <ArticleTitle>Left main coronary artery occlusion in an asymptomatic patient: late complication after arterial switch operation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>599-600</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/jocs.12785</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Long-term complications of the arterial switch operation for transposition of the great arteries include coronary artery stenosis and occlusion. We present a patient with high-grade left main coronary artery stenosis 18 years following the arterial switch procedure who was successfully treated with a left internal mammary artery to left anterior descending artery bypass.</AbstractText>
